      "hideComponent": "false",
      "jcr:created": "Tue Jan 21 2025 20:08:44 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #323232;\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">APP Guidance</span></span></span></span></h2>\n<h1><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Identifying and educating mild<sup>®</sup> patients</span></span></h1>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><b>Publish date:</b> March 2, 2026</span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Feb 19 2026 16:30:50 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
    "text_copy_copy_copy__877216131": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "bottomPadding": "1",
      "topPadding": "1",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Does your practice offer the mild<sup>®</sup> procedure? Do you manage patient identification and education? Consider following these 3 steps to optimize your practice routine:<br>\n &nbsp;</span></p>\n<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">1. Start with the symptoms</span></span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>ID shopping cart syndrome</b><br>\n Shopping Cart Syndrome – lumbar spinal stenosis (LSS) with neurogenic claudication (NC). These patients will often be the first ones to find chairs in your waiting room or use the walking aids, such as a shopping cart, to establish a flexed position. The flexed posture is a common sign of NC because it opens up the spinal canal to alleviate the pressure on the central canal to avoid pain that comes with being straight, upright, or mobile.<sup>1</sup></span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Feb 19 2026 16:28:30 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
    "cols2_copy_195156014_1245133517": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 20 2025 14:57:52 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 20 2025 14:57:52 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
          "preset": "max_width_1440",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Nov 26 2025 14:40:14 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "Patients suffering from lumbar spinal stenosis (LSS) will often be the first ones to find chairs in your waiting room or use the walking aids, such as a shopping cart, to establish a flexed position",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/ivs/news/app-blogs/identifying-and-educating mild® patients/images/mild_shopping-cart-syndrome-rev.png",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Nov 26 2025 20:41:31 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys"
      }
    },
    "text_copy_copy_copy__2134062622": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "bottomPadding": "1",
      "topPadding": "0",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "topMargin": "-2",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">LSS with NC patients may present with limited mobility from the onset of symptoms. Patients commonly report pain and may have functional limitations. The functional limitations can include a desire to walk the dog, get the mail, and play with their grandchildren.</span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Feb 03 2026 14:04:41 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
    "text_copy_copy_copy__74857892": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "bottomPadding": "1",
      "topPadding": "1",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">2. Possible signs and symptoms of a typical mild<sup>®</sup> patient</span></span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Look for the ligament</b> <br>\n Hypertrophic ligamentum flavum (HLF) contributes up to 85% of spinal canal narrowing<sup>2</sup></span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Feb 19 2026 16:28:43 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
    "cols2_copy_195156014": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-4a9aa678a2@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 20 2025 14:57:52 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 20 2025 14:57:52 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
